          <item>Use part (a) to show that, for odd powers of sine, $$\int_{0}^{\pi \slash 2}{\sin^{2n + 1}xdx = \frac{2 \cdot 4 \cdot 6 \cdot \cdot \cdot \cdot \cdot 2n}{3 \cdot 5 \cdot 7 \cdot \cdot \cdot \cdot \cdot \left( {2n + 1} \right)}}$$</item>
